# Assistant instructions — PILAR-2b (CP2B Maps V3)

## What this is
Biogas and biomethane potential of São Paulo's 645 municipalities, with a beta
national layer.
- `frontend/`: Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, next-intl (pt-BR and en),
  Leaflet, React Query.
- `backend/`: FastAPI and psycopg2 on PostgreSQL + PostGIS.
- Production: the Unicamp VM (Apache → PM2: backend :8001, frontend :3002).
  See `docs/VM_UPDATE_GUIDE.md`.
- Local: Docker Compose, or `scripts/verify-local.sh`. See
  `docs/qa/LOCAL_VERIFICATION.md`.

## Rules the checks enforce
- No user-facing text in code: it goes in `frontend/messages/{pt-BR,en}.json`.
  Every `t('key')` is type-checked, and `npm run i18n:check` fails on
  hardcoded Portuguese and on unused keys (`docs/architecture/I18N_GUIDE.md`).
- Numbers and dates on screen go through `useFormat()` (`src/lib/format.ts`),
  never `toFixed` or `toLocaleString`.
- Markup built as a string (Leaflet popups, tooltips, divIcons) passes every
  value through `escapeHtml` (`src/lib/html.ts`).
- A modal uses `useDialog` (Escape, focus, a `role="dialog"` named by its title).
- API errors answer with a fixed message and log the exception, never
  `detail=str(e)` (`backend/tests/unit/test_error_details.py`).
- A request-derived value in a log message goes through `log_safe`
  (`backend/app/core/log_sanitizer.py`).
- Migrations: numbered, re-runnable, never edited once applied
  (`backend/app/migrations/README.md`).

## Before pushing
```bash
(cd frontend && npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run i18n:check && npm test \
  && npm run build && git checkout -- next-env.d.ts)
(cd backend && black . --check && isort . --check-only \
  && flake8 app/ --max-line-length=100 --extend-ignore=E203,W503 && pytest)
```
Run from the NewLook directory; each line is a subshell, so the second starts
there too. `next build` rewrites `next-env.d.ts`, hence the checkout.
`npm run typecheck` covers the tests and e2e specs too. Backend CI runs
`tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/compliance` (pytest.ini), so new
tests go there.

## Conventions
- Code and identifiers in English; comments in the language of the file.
- Extend the shared helpers (`lib/format`, `lib/html`, `hooks/useDialog`,
  `log_safe`) rather than writing another copy.
- WCAG 2.1 AA: labelled controls, keyboard access, no colour-only meaning.
- Small commits, each with the tests that prove it; say what was verified.
